ture or planeswalker would die this turn, exile it instead.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2024-11-15","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":0.0,"color_identity":["B"],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"","name":"Swamp","oracle_id":"56719f6a-1a6c-4c0a-8d21-18f7d7350b68","oracle_text":"({T}: Add {B}.)","power":null,"produced_mana":["B"],"released_at":"2026-06-26","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Land — Swamp"},{"cmc":0.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"","name":"Wastes","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","oracle_text":"{T}: Add {C}.","power":null,"produced_mana":["C"],"released_at":"2025-08-01","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Land"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Because Wastes is a basic land, you can include as many of them as you like in your Constructed decks.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In Limited events (including Sealed Deck and Booster Draft), Wastes must be in your card pool to be included in your deck. You can't add Wastes to your card pool in the same way that you can add other basic lands.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Wastes is not a land type. If something asks you to name a land type, you can't choose Wastes.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A card with devoid is just colorless. It's not colorless and the colors of mana in its mana cost.","oracle_id":"46515251-2172-4b0a-81ac-4c0120b73360","published_at":"2024-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Devoid doesn't affect the color identity of the card for the purposes of the Commander variant. For example, while Abstruse Appropriation is colorless because it has devoid, its color identity is still white and black, and it can't be included in a Commander deck where the commander's color identity doesn't include both white and black.","oracle_id":"46515251-2172-4b0a-81ac-4c0120b73360","published_at":"2024-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Devoid works in all zones, not just on the battlefield.","oracle_id":"46515251-2172-4b0a-81ac-4c0120b73360","published_at":"2024-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a card loses devoid, it will still be colorless. This is because effects that change an object's color (like the one created by devoid) are considered before the object loses devoid.","oracle_id":"46515251-2172-4b0a-81ac-4c0120b73360","published_at":"2024-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Other cards and abilities can give a card with devoid a color. If that happens, it's just the new color, not that color and colorless.","oracle_id":"46515251-2172-4b0a-81ac-4c0120b73360","published_at":"2024-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The replacement effect of Fanged Flames will exile the target creature or planeswalker if it would die this turn for any reason, not just due to lethal damage.","oracle_id":"46515251-2172-4b0a-81ac-4c0120b73360","published_at":"2024-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Obliterating Bolt's replacement effect will exile the target creature if it would die this turn for any reason, not just due to lethal damage.","oracle_id":"57fe941c-a830-4570-afe2-18f93c7a7b84","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A creature or planeswalker dealt damage this way will be exiled instead of dying if it dies for any reason later in the turn, even if it initially survived the 2 damage.","oracle_id":"6a521eed-0965-4fce-8a11-190dc2863da8","published_at":"2021-11-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If there are fewer than twenty cards in the targeted player's library, that player puts all the cards from their library into their graveyard.","oracle_id":"cc2b6e58-2d6f-495e-95f3-9496105c4cba","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Scorching Dragonfire's replacement effect will exile the target creature or planeswalker if it would die this turn for any reason, not just due to lethal damage. It applies to the target creature or planeswalker even if Scorching Dragonfire deals no damage to it (most likely due to a prevention effect).","oracle_id":"d14f313c-fea6-49c4-8197-5b74ee584a6b","published_at":"2019-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Scorching Dragonfire's replacement effect will exile the target creature or planeswalker if it would die this turn for any reason, not just due to lethal damage.","oracle_id":"d14f313c-fea6-49c4-8197-5b74ee584a6b","published_at":"2020-06-23","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Scorching Dragonfire's replacement effect will exile the target creature or planeswalker if it would die this turn for any reason, not just due to lethal damage.","oracle_id":"d14f313c-fea6-49c4-8197-5b74ee584a6b","published_at":"2024-09-20","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
